    "Defend and hit change arm/body posture; turns show distinct rear and side equipment; death folds and topples the pressure body into the matching final corpse. No essential body part touches the full450x400 native canvas edges.",
    "Directional melee11/12/13 uses the smaller working arm rather than treating a projectile as melee. Shoot14/15/16 aims the pressure nozzle up/level/down and paints charge/release/recovery; green rim moves a few source/native pixels with the painted barrel recoil. Frame4 nozzle landmarks are close to documented projectile release5 anchor. This is source alignment evidence only, not observed native projectile timing.",
    "Green is localized to reagent glass and charged nozzle. Weathered brown metal remains readable; purple connectors are restrained and do not override the machine material. Upgrade hardware is more substantial than the base concept. Final side-by-side base/upgrade and moving in-game approval remain pending.",
